                <pb facs="0722" n="614" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg614"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.5112 France/16: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Herrick</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-06-10T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 10, 1927—2
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>172. Tour telegram No. 231, June 2, 9 p.m. According to <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >New York Times</hi> today Briand has made his proposal in definite form and
                    on June 3 gave you a note explaining his idea of how the pact should be framed.
                    It was also stated that the note has been forwarded to Washington.</p>
                <p>The Department wishes to be informed whether such a note has been received. If it
                    has, please telegraph summary of contents.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
